   "id": "vo02",
   "text": "In the pan on the stove, a few kernels of popcorn sit still. Then one jumps. Its hard shell holds the steam in, until the pressure wins. It pops when it gets to about one hundred eighty degrees Celsius. The pop is over in a few thousandths of a second. Here, that's a few seconds. The shell splits, and the white foam bursts out. That crack you'd hear is the shell giving way. One kernel becomes a fluffy cloud, many times its size. The foam hangs for a moment, then settles in the pan. Over the sink, a soap bubble drifts, about as wide as an egg. Its colors swirl as the wall of the bubble thins. When it pops, the hole races around the film at several meters a second. The whole bubble is gone in about a hundredth of a second. Here, that takes about eleven seconds. And somebody across the kitchen has just clapped. How long does that take to reach you?",
   "heard": "In the pan on the stove, a few kernels of popcorn sit still. Then one jumps. Its hard shell holds the steam in until the pressure wins. It pops when it gets to about 180 degrees Celsius. The pop is over in a few thousandths of a second. Here, that's a few seconds. The shell splits, and the white foam bursts out. That crack you'd hear is the shell giving way. One kernel becomes a fluffy cloud, many times its size. The foam hangs for a moment, then settles in the pan. Over the sink, a soap bubble drifts about as wide as an egg. Its colors swirl as the wall of the bubble thins. When it pops, the hole races around the film at several meters a second. The whole bubble is gone in about a hundredth of a second. Here, that takes about eleven seconds, and somebody across the kitchen has just clapped. How long does that take to reach you?",
